  "title": "Dresden – Bodenbach und Tetschen und zurück",
  "notes": "Winter 1913/14, pp. 68-71 (four pages; summer had six). Down (p1 p68, p2 p69): rows 0-29 and 30-59, kept \"aus Dresden Hbf.\" (r0, r30), \"in Bodenbach\" (r14, r44), \"in Tetschen\" (r24, r54). Up (p3 p70, p4 p71): rows 60-103 and 104-146 from the connection rows at the top; kept \"a. Tetschen\" (r65, r109), \"aus Bodenbach\" (r78, r121), \"in Dresden Hbf.\" (r92, r135); the header band lies among skipped rows (it is printed below the a. Tetschen row), as in the summer layout. Columns of dashes only (p2 c24-c25, p4 c48-c51) are kept as columns. Deskew by hand (-0.84, 0, -0.87, 0.25 deg): pp. 68, 70 and 71 are sheared (rules and lines of times are not square), so the angle is a compromise that keeps rows within about 1 px and rules within about 2 px. Each page has a footnote box (Vorortzüge line; p69 the Zollabfertigung notes; p70 the D 67 note; p71 the Elsterwerda and 1 April notes)."
